  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This problem has subtasks.\n\nAlice and Bob are playing a game with a binary string SSS of length NNN. The game involves two steps:\n\n\nAlice's Move: Alice can remove any single substring from SSS. The remaining parts of the string stay in the same order.\nBob's Move: After Alice's move, Bob can select any substring of the modified string and flip all its characters. Flipping SiS_iSi​ means it becomes 111 if it was originally 000, and vice versa.The game ends after that.\nIf both players make their moves optimally, with Alice aiming to maximize the lexicographical value of the final string and Bob aiming to minimize it, what will be the resulting string?\n\nNote:\n\n\n\nThe empty subsequence is lexicographically the smallest of all.\n\n\n\n\nA substring of a string is obtained by deleting some (possibly zero) characters from the beginning and some (possibly zero) characters from the end. Thus, an **empty string is also a valid substring** of SSS.\n\n\n\n\nString XXX is lexicographically smaller than string YYY, if either of the following satisfies:\n\n\n\nXXX is a prefix of YYY and X≠YX \\neq YX=Y.\nThere exists an index iii such that Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​ and Xj=Yj,∀jX_j = Y_j, \\forall jXj​=Yj​,∀j such that 1≤j&lt;i1 \\leq j \\lt i1≤j&lt;i.\n\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN — the length of SSS.\nThe next line contains the binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the final string SSS.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "SSS is a binary string, i.e, contains only the characters 000 and 111.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 111 (202020 points):** The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 500050005000.",
      "**Subtask 222 (808080 points):** No further constraints."
    ],
